@title Live view: hold a pushbutton (wide window)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# The wide window docks the Pages list, so the card sits further right.
# mouse_down on an Operate button holds it: the row reads "pressed", the
# button is lit and the contactor pulls in; mouse_up lets it go. Two things
# used to drop the press: the button's id moved when a line appeared above it
# (after one frame), and egui stops counting a plain click sense as pressed
# after 0.8 s. The second picture is taken 40 frames later (about 2 s) to show
# the hold survives both.
click_text "Open example"
wait 20
key shift+l
wait 20
try click_text "Go to page 2 Control circuit"
wait 20
move 322 397
wait 3
mouse_down 322 397
wait 2
shot held-early
expect "push button · pressed"
expect "pulled in"
wait 40
shot held-later
expect "push button · pressed"
mouse_up 322 397
wait 5
expect_not "push button · pressed"
shot released
